  "body": "### Summary\nAs a reader who follows links between topics, I want to see how many readers are stacked behind the one on screen, so that I know how far back I am, as in the published app.\n\nMilestone: M4 (operator, 2026-11-08). Found by the `2440d79..2fe43da3` sweep of #655 (row `602b900e`), opened by its catch-up pass.\n\n### Legacy @ `2fe43da3` (`legacy/duo-inner-cover`, #372)\n- A reader pushed from a link has `navigationDepth + 1`. When the depth is above 0, the title shows a small capsule (chevron and the depth, white on the action tint) before the topic title, accessibility label \"N affichage de messages empilé\" (`HFRswift/Swift/MessagesView.swift:3410-3440` @ `2fe43da3`, `602b900e`).\n- At `2440d79` the same count was in a custom back button (`navigationDepthBackButton`, `MessagesView.swift:4238-4265` @ `2440d79`); `602b900e` moved it into the title and dropped the \"back to root\" button.\n\n### Current SwiftHFR\nA followed link pushes a new reader (`TopicReaderModel.linkedReader`, LOT-137); the reader's title is `model.title` (`App/SwiftHFR/Reader/TopicReaderView.swift:89`), with no depth count. LOT-137's spec does not list this as a difference.\n\n### Scope\n- The depth indicator next to the title of a pushed reader, same rule (shown when depth > 0), same accessibility label.\n- Nothing else of the reader's title changes.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- Depth 0: no indicator. Depth 1, 2: the count, updated on back.\n- A unit test on the depth given to each pushed reader; light, dark and Dynamic Type XL checked on a Mac.\n",
